{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce","id":1534199,"title":"Gangrel = Old Clan Tzimisce","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-14T10:26:02-07:00","id":1534199,"title":"Gangrel = Old Clan Tzimisce","content":"The thought occurred to me that it would be interesting if the Old Clan Tzimisce are the Gangrel. There were always a-political Gangrel roving the wilderness - but more politically minded Gangrel become rural lords - predatory owners of the land and its subjects. Lacking common mind control Disciplines, these lordly Gangrel focus on blood bonds and breeding ghoul families to serve them. Dracula was one of these, having the Protean Discipline as the book shows.<br /> <br /> When Tzimisce join the Sabbat, they lose their closeness to nature and over time Protean morphs into Vicissitude. Independent Gangrel continue roaming the woods, but the more politically minded Gangrel (Old Clan Tzimisce) who are hyper conservative elders who are extremely territorial join with the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> The standard Tzimisce, then, are regarded as Tzimisce antitribu by the Camarilla Gangrel. These Camarilla Gangrel are more political than in canon, being like the Old Clan Tzimisce and favor complete obedience to elders, the sanctity of domain, utilize ghoul (and revenant) servants. <br /> <br /> What does everybody think of this alternative viewpoint?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T10:50:59-07:00","id":1534200,"title":"","content":"I would split the difference by suggesting that the Gangrel and Tzimisce share the same 2nd Generation ancestor. Though the Old Clan Tzimisce to Gangrel concept falls apart somewhat with the whole Koldunic sorcery aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T11:02:22-07:00","id":1534202,"title":"","content":"Its a different idea even if I'm not sold on it.<br /> <br /> The merits I can see are fewer clans, which means the clans can be broader in concept and that fleshcraft is less spread out in very focused forms and can be tied together in a single shapeshifting Discipline. Especially if you divest the Setites from Serpentis you can have the Gangrel as the only Shapeshifting clan which in turn allows them to be, as I mentioned above, broader in concepts.<br /> <br /> The negative parts I see is that the way shapeshifting is spread between Gangrel, Tzimisce and Setites you can also get more focused, if narrower in concept, clans. From my personal perspective I am pretty set in my ways I'm not sure that I would want, or my players could accept a change of this magnitude to the setting. So there's a conservative reaction to these changes that could make it less attractive even if it technically would be an improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T12:16:34-07:00","id":1534208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce?p=1534200#post1534200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would split the difference by suggesting that the Gangrel and Tzimisce share the same 2nd Generation ancestor. Though the Old Clan Tzimisce to Gangrel concept falls apart somewhat with the whole Koldunic sorcery aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Gangre could learn Koldunic Sorcery, just like some Tzimisce learned it. I don\u2019t think it would be so different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce?p=1534202#post1534202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a different idea even if I'm not sold on it.<br /> <br /> The merits I can see are fewer clans, which means the clans can be broader in concept and that fleshcraft is less spread out in very focused forms and can be tied together in a single shapeshifting Discipline. Especially if you divest the Setites from Serpentis you can have the Gangrel as the only Shapeshifting clan which in turn allows them to be, as I mentioned above, broader in concepts.<br /> <br /> The negative parts I see is that the way shapeshifting is spread between Gangrel, Tzimisce and Setites you can also get more focused, if narrower in concept, clans. From my personal perspective I am pretty set in my ways I'm not sure that I would want, or my players could accept a change of this magnitude to the setting. So there's a conservative reaction to these changes that could make it less attractive even if it technically would be an improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if I were doing a more complete Clan simplification, I would do something different entirely with the Setites. Maybe combine them with Lasombra and/or Baali and make Obtenebration their Discipline. <br /> <br /> Back to the Tzimisce and Gangrel. I do think that this change would be unpopular with some, for conservatism I\u2019d for no other reason.<br /> <br /> I find it to be kind of elegant, that is just me. One advantage I see is that by incorporating the Old Clan Tzimisce concept into the Gangrel it gives the Camarilla Gangrel a bit more to do. It makes them more of a part of the Camarilla political landscape and a reason to be there. It\u2019s kind of like adding OC Tzimisce to the Camarilla without the baggage of another Clan being there. Canon Gangrel were always a little bit out of place in the Camarilla - since they were so focused on wilderness and/or being nomadic that they didn\u2019t have a big role in the political landscape of the Camarilla. - which is likely why they are made independent in later editions. Making them OCT creates this other political faction in the Camarilla and allows those interesting OCT ideas to be used more completely.<br /> <br /> Those are just my thoughts on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T14:54:36-07:00","id":1534212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce#post1534199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thought occurred to me that it would be interesting if the Old Clan Tzimisce are the Gangrel. There were always a-political Gangrel roving the wilderness - but more politically minded Gangrel become rural lords - predatory owners of the land and its subjects. Lacking common mind control Disciplines, these lordly Gangrel focus on blood bonds and breeding ghoul families to serve them. Dracula was one of these, having the Protean Discipline as the book shows.<br /> <br /> When Tzimisce join the Sabbat, they lose their closeness to nature and over time Protean morphs into Vicissitude. Independent Gangrel continue roaming the woods, but the more politically minded Gangrel (Old Clan Tzimisce) who are hyper conservative elders who are extremely territorial join with the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The standard Tzimisce, then, are regarded as Tzimisce antitribu by the Camarilla Gangrel. These Camarilla Gangrel are more political than in canon, being like the Old Clan Tzimisce and favor complete obedience to elders, the sanctity of domain, utilize ghoul (and revenant) servants.<br /> <br /> What does everybody think of this alternative viewpoint?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but it seems pointless. It's an interesting story point, but you would need to develop more than that to make any difference otherwise it just don't make diference..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T18:03:50-07:00","id":1534219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce?p=1534212#post1534212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but it seems pointless. It's an interesting story point, but you would need to develop more than that to make any difference otherwise it just don't make diference..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well, that\u2019s just like, uh, your opinion man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T05:10:23-07:00","id":1534244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce?p=1534219#post1534219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, well, that\u2019s just like, uh, your opinion man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like everyone else, but then, can you explain to me how this makes any difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T11:16:11-07:00","id":1534257,"title":"","content":"It would be different to say the least and did do something like it in the Reqiem line? I only ask as I always thought they would make a natural fit with the Nosferatu as a bloodline as ancenstral horrors and seekers of dark horrible lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T11:49:47-07:00","id":1534260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce?p=1534257#post1534257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be different to say the least and did do something like it in the Reqiem line? I only ask as I always thought they would make a natural fit with the Nosferatu as a bloodline as ancenstral horrors and seekers of dark horrible lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think that the Tzimisce could be a Nosferatu Bloodline? I think that would be an interesting twist. It goes with the more monstrous depictions of Tzimisce appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T15:06:19-07:00","id":1534270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce?p=1534260#post1534260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You think that the Tzimisce could be a Nosferatu Bloodline? I think that would be an interesting twist. It goes with the more monstrous depictions of Tzimisce appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would make more sense if it were the other way around and the Nosferatu clan was a Tzimice bloodline, originating from a failed experiment (or not) with vicissitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T16:22:51-07:00","id":1534272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce?p=1534260#post1534260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You think that the Tzimisce could be a Nosferatu Bloodline? I think that would be an interesting twist. It goes with the more monstrous depictions of Tzimisce appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>When we started playing the VTR line and we got into what VTM clans could fit as a bloodline and making the Fiends as a Nosferatu bloodline was a better fit then making them a Gangrel or Ventrue bloodline in the other game setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T13:31:56-07:00","id":1534305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce?p=1534260#post1534260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You think that the Tzimisce could be a Nosferatu Bloodline? I think that would be an interesting twist. It goes with the more monstrous depictions of Tzimisce appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just seemed a more natural fit in VTR then say the Gangrel or the Ventrue in that game line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T12:13:48-07:00","id":1534502,"title":"","content":"Yes Sergeant Brother though the discipline spread would be some trouble to go with. Do I want Dominate or Protean to the spread as Nightmare is cool power to go with and I lean more towards the Dominate power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T09:06:37-07:00","id":1534559,"title":"","content":"If one would run the Tzimisce as a Nosferatu bloodline I would suggest that the Fiends are actually divided into several different bloodlines to get a more focused concept for each. And perhaps tie them together in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Like Kolduns becomes one bloodline, crazy fleshcrafters and Metamorphosis becomes one, tyrannical lords becomes another. And I think that's it. You could presumably name them after the Tzimisce ghoul families in the VtM lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T22:06:34-07:00","id":1536923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534199-gangrel-old-clan-tzimisce#post1534199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thought occurred to me that it would be interesting if the Old Clan Tzimisce are the Gangrel. There were always a-political Gangrel roving the wilderness - but more politically minded Gangrel become rural lords - predatory owners of the land and its subjects. Lacking common mind control Disciplines, these lordly Gangrel focus on blood bonds and breeding ghoul families to serve them. Dracula was one of these, having the Protean Discipline as the book shows.<br /> <br /> When Tzimisce join the Sabbat, they lose their closeness to nature and over time Protean morphs into Vicissitude. Independent Gangrel continue roaming the woods, but the more politically minded Gangrel (Old Clan Tzimisce) who are hyper conservative elders who are extremely territorial join with the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The standard Tzimisce, then, are regarded as Tzimisce antitribu by the Camarilla Gangrel. These Camarilla Gangrel are more political than in canon, being like the Old Clan Tzimisce and favor complete obedience to elders, the sanctity of domain, utilize ghoul (and revenant) servants.<br /> <br /> What does everybody think of this alternative viewpoint?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can do whatever you want. The metaplot is intentionally ambiguous for this very reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}